IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`

-- ccc7-s183-offence.l4 -- the definition of "offence" in section 183 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part VI, Invasion of Privacy): the offences for which this Part
-- lets an authorization be given and the rules of this Part apply, as a table of the provisions the text lists, plus the lead-in ("an offence contrary to, any conspiracy or attempt to commit or being
-- an accessory after the fact in relation to an offence contrary to, or any counselling in relation to an offence contrary to") and the closing words ("and includes any other offence that there are
-- reasonable grounds to believe is ...").
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- GENERATED by work/gen_offence.py from the text (never retyped); the rows are in the text's order. Two rows of (a) are shown repealed in this text: (xxxiv) and (xxxv) to (xxxviii): they have no row of the table.
--
-- Where the table lives. Paragraph (a) lists provisions of the Criminal Code; paragraphs (b) to (k) list provisions of other Acts, and (e.1) and (j) name a whole Act. The core's `Provision of the Code` cannot name an Act,
-- so this module declares `s 183 provision of an Act` (recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md); `s 183 provision of the Criminal Code` turns a core record into one. The core record also cannot name a paragraph:
-- FORK (F3): the one paragraph the text lists, 202(1)(e), is carried as the subsection "(1)(e)" (recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md); a charge under 202(1) that does not say which paragraph is not in the table.
-- "subsection 83.03(1)" is a row of its own from "subsection 83.03(2)": the reach is the subsection named, not the section.

§ `Section 183 "offence" -- the table`

DECLARE `s 183 statute` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 the Criminal Code`
    `s 183 the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act`
    `s 183 the Biological and Toxin Weapons Convention Implementation Act`
    `s 183 the Cannabis Act`
    `s 183 the Competition Act`
    `s 183 the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
    `s 183 the Copyright Act`
    `s 183 the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`
    `s 183 the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act`
    `s 183 the Customs Act`
    `s 183 the Excise Act, 2001`
    `s 183 the Export and Import Permits Act`
    `s 183 the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`
    `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`
    `s 183 the Trademarks Act`
    `s 183 an Act that is none of those`

DECLARE `s 183 reach of a listed provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 the whole section`
    `s 183 the subsection or paragraph named`
    `s 183 every offence under the Act`

-- The provision a charge is under: the Act, the section as a decimal (380; 83.02; 462.31) and the subsection or paragraph as the text writes it ("" or "(1)", "(3.1)", "(1)(e)").
DECLARE `s 183 provision of an Act` HAS
    `statute`      IS A `s 183 statute`
    `section`      IS A NUMBER
    `subsection`   IS A STRING

GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A `s 183 provision of an Act`
`s 183 provision of the Criminal Code` MEANS
    `s 183 provision of an Act` WITH `statute` IS `s 183 the Criminal Code`, `section` IS p's `section`, `subsection` IS p's `subsection`

DECLARE `s 183 row of the list of offences` HAS
    `label`        IS A STRING
    `statute`      IS A `s 183 statute`
    `reach`        IS A `s 183 reach of a listed provision`
    `section`      IS A NUMBER
    `subsection`   IS A STRING

